IDEAS

This folder keeps the ideas we find in other terminals: what they do well
that tam-last should learn from, and what they do badly that tam-last
should avoid.


ONE FILE PER TERMINAL

  <name>.md, for example foot.md or kitty.md. Each file has:

    What it is           language, licence, libraries, scope
    Ideas worth taking   each with a verdict and a reason
    Things to avoid      each with a reason
    Where to look        files or docs to read when we act on an idea

  Verdicts:

    adopt     we want this; it has (or will get) a place in a plan
    consider  promising; needs a closer look or Fred's view
    reject    we decided against it, and the reason says why

  An idea that tam-last builds gets the plan or version that delivered it,
  for example "adopt (P1, 0.0.1)". When code is taken, not just the idea,
  it is also recorded in UPSTREAM.md.

  synthesis.md gathers the best ideas from every file by topic, and is the
  place to start.


REFERENCE CLONES

  sources lists the terminals and libraries we keep a local clone of, so
  we can read their code and follow their fixes. tools/pull-references brings every listed
  clone up to date and clones any that are missing:

    tools/pull-references          pull every listed clone
    tools/pull-references --list   show what is listed and where

  The clones live outside this repository (under ~/Code). Nothing is ever
  pushed or posted to those projects.


HOW DEEP THESE NOTES GO

  foot, havoc, st and kitty's keyboard protocol were read from source on
  2026-11-17 (commits in UPSTREAM.md). ghostty, alacritty and wezterm
  were looked through for their structure only; xterm and the Linux
  console are starter notes from their documentation. Notes not read
  from source say so, and are checked against source before we act on
  them. A full "survey the field" happens only when Fred asks for one.
